/-!
# KFW C-layer 5: core registers, level frames, the top kernels

Registers of the uniform Proposition 14 core (all `< 56`, outside `gT` and `pT`):

  `1 K`, `3 S`, `4 r`, `5 H`, `19 ES k`, `20 B'`, `21 P`, `22 D`, `23 ρ`, `27 k`, `28 q₀`,
  `29 D' = D - q₀`, `32 m^k`;

scratch registers `2, 6 … 18` (the level frame `2, 6 … 10`, loop registers `11 … 15`, tests
`16, 17`, the scale `18`).

* `BaseR`, `CoreR`: the register facts; `CoreR.push`: pushes on scratch registers keep them.
* `levR_frame`: a level frame on top of the core registers is a `LevR`.
* **`topQ`**: the recursive procedure `topC` implements the kernels `C` on the bits
  `i ≤ x < q₀` of the layer, by level-`0` calls.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

